        {
          "id": 1714771968,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This strikes me as a case where either choice default would not match some people's use scenarios.  As a libpcap and libwiretap developer, I mainly use it to look at the file structure rather than the packets.\n\n> Wanted this behavior when PCAPNG example is GRE encapsulated in custom protocol,\n\nSo, in that case, why would you have Wireshark dissect the pcapng file as a file rather than just read it as a capture?  How is the pcapng-level content relevant?",
